Original commit body from 18fff11b429bb99c181306d315d0f3910f5d0b7f:

_taint_blind_reason withheld a clean verdict from EVERY taint claim when any
language in the repo had no taint catalogue and made production calls. For a
label a project's own source catalogue declares in specific languages, a
language it is not declared in cannot be where such a flow starts.

- taint.source_origin_languages: None for a built-in label (any language can
  produce untrusted_input / host_secret / the crypto labels, so the gate is
  unchanged for them), else the languages the catalogue declares the label in.
- cli._languages_a_flow_can_be_in: adds every language a present
  cross-language call edge enters (java -> kotlin on one JVM). Edges only
  ADD a language; their absence is never trusted, which is the fail-open
  reachability form WI-rusil rejects.
- _taint_blind_reason(source_languages=...) scopes the EDGE LIST, so the
  no-catalogue census and the coverage check walk one population (INV-motos).
- A verdict that set a language aside names it in its details.

Controls (WI-rusil's three): a label declared in the uncatalogued language
is still withheld (fixture, and on postal with a ruby-declared label); the
self-proof is byte-identical (18 confirmed_with_caveats, no flip); built-in
labels are unchanged (sherpa-onnx byte-identical, and all 353 withheld
corpus verdicts carry built-in labels).

